{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419796-curse-weak-target-affect-resistant-target-secondarily-raw","id":1419796,"title":"Curse weak target, affect resistant target secondarily? RAW","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-23T08:51:27-07:00","id":1419796,"title":"Curse weak target, affect resistant target secondarily? RAW","content":"The Mind Sphere is the best example for this question, because it depends on a variable trait. Willpower tends to range between three and ten (max). Mind 3, Entopy3, Forces 2 &quot;You will draw the ire of all who see your face&quot;-curse. Target has 3 willpower. Hexer gets five successes, then leaves the area. A sleeper with the willpower 10 and Iron Will merit enters the scene where the cursed target remains. The two meet. For reference:<br /> <br /> Caster is Luaxana, the Euthanatos witch.<br /> Target is Billy, the hapless sleeper.<br /> Third party is Jenna, the un-awakened monk (She can't detect the effect through Spheres, has perception 1 and awareness 0).<br /> <br /> Is Jenna's disposition toward Billy dictated by the predetermined curse-effect already cast? <br /> <br /> If not, is the difficulty of casting the effect based on the average willpower of those Billy would meet in his travels until the end of the effect's duration? Other variable?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T10:04:01-07:00","id":1419805,"title":"","content":"Not quite. &quot;You will draw the ire of all who see your face&quot; obviously affects the minds of &quot;all who see your face&quot;. And Mind spells default to Vulgarity/Witnesses for the difficulty when the effect affects more than one person.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20 p.519</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For attacks against multiple targets, the difficulty for a Mind-based Effect depends upon the usual coincidental, vulgar, or vulgar with witnesses situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>It still does generate the oddity of being easier to affect Jenna alongside Billy than Jenna alone, because the difficulty isn't likely to be 10 (keep in mind, though, that if the mood change it's ovious, Jenna could be entitled to a Will based &quot;dodge&quot;).<br /> <br /> A possible house rule you could make for this not to be the case, would be to allow the Mage to set the difficulty, and then say that the spell affects only those whose Will it's equal or less than the number chossen","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T11:28:39-07:00","id":1419821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419796-curse-weak-target-affect-resistant-target-secondarily-raw?p=1419805#post1419805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;You will draw the ire of all who see your face&quot; obviously affects the minds of &quot;all who see your face&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple logic, overlooked.<br /> Perfect. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 10-23-2020, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}